  "result": "I've found the likely cause and written a plan, but I haven't changed any code because plan mode is on.\n\nIn `--help`, each option's names are listed with the longer ones first (`--help, -h`). The usual order is short first (`-h, --help`). The cause is `reverse=True` in the sort in `join_options`, at `src/click/formatting.py:319`.\n\n**Proposed fix:**\n- Remove `reverse=True` from that sort. Names with the same prefix length keep the order you declared them in.\n- Add a regression test for the ordering, for example `join_options([\"--help\", \"-h\"])` should return `\"-h, --help\"`.\n- Add a line to `CHANGES.md`.\n- Run the test suite to check nothing else depends on the old order.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-steady-wreath.md`. I couldn't find a tool here to formally request plan approval. If you approve, I'll make the change.",
